    {
      "id": "ticket_to",
      "target": "Билет до ___, пожалуйста.",
      "pronunciation_easy": "bee-LYET dah, pah-ZHAH-loo-stah",
      "qa": "До takes the genitive (до аэропорта, до вокзала). For trains/buses between cities, the city name also goes in the genitive: до Москвы."
    },
    {
      "id": "does_this_go_to",
      "target": "Этот идёт до ___?",
      "pronunciation_easy": "EH-tat ee-DYOT dah",
      "qa": "Lit. 'Does this one go to ___?', said pointing at a bus or train (автобус, поезд, трамвай are masculine). For a commuter train (электричка, feminine) it would be Эта идёт до ___? To a driver: Вы едете до ___? (Are you going to ___?). Not sure which is best as a single default."
    },
    {
      "id": "take_me_to",
      "target": "Довезите меня до ___, пожалуйста.",
      "pronunciation_easy": "dah-vee-ZEE-tyeh mee-NYAH dah, pah-ZHAH-loo-stah",
      "qa": "Lit. 'Drive me as far as ___, please' (taxi). До always takes the genitive. Отвезите меня в/на ___ is equally natural but its preposition changes per place (в аэропорт, на вокзал), so до was chosen to keep the frame fixed. In practice drivers also accept just 'До аэропорта, пожалуйста.'"
    },
